  "skeleton": "a fishing boat seen from the side, bow to the right: root under the keel; hull on it (wheelhouse, mast, crossbar, rigging); net (the bundled net with its floats and the rope it hangs by) on a bone where that rope ties to the mast, swinging out and hauled up; an open-net variant.",
